      "body": "### Motivation\n\nIn environments where routed NVLS multicast mapping is unavailable (such as inside multi-GPU Confidential Computing VMs),  raises  unconditionally during model initialization.\nUnlike other multicast consumers (such as  and ), which catch the error and gracefully fall back, the K3 latent-MoE tail fusion had no fallback, preventing Kimi K3 from running on SM100 in CC environments even though the portable non-fused latent-MoE path works properly.\n\nFixes #65568.\n\n### Proposed Changes\n\nCatch  during  in , log a warning, and gracefully disable tail fusion (, ) to fall back to the standard non-fused latent-MoE tail.\n",
